 "drivingQuestion": "How can an eiruv placed outside the limit be effective?",
 "outcome": "resolved",
 "outcomeNote": "resolved by emendation",
 "continuesQuestionOf": null,
 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "eruvin.60b.6",
   "daf": "60b",
   "sentenceId": 5,
   "he": "הַנּוֹתֵן עֵירוּבוֹ בְּתוֹךְ עִיבּוּרָהּ וְכוּ׳. חוּץ לַתְּחוּם סָלְקָא דַּעְתָּךְ? אֶלָּא אֵימָא: חוּץ לְעִיבּוּרָהּ.",
   "en": "We learned in the mishna: «One who places his eiruv within the outskirts» of the city has not accomplished anything. However, if he places it outside the city limits, it is effective. The Gemara expresses surprise: «Can it enter your mind» that the mishna is dealing with a case where one placed his eiruv «outside the» Shabbat «limit?» If the eiruv is outside the Shabbat limit as measured from his physical location at the onset of Shabbat, he cannot access it on Shabbat; it is therefore ineffective in establishing his Shabbat residence. «Rather,» correct it and «say» as follows: If one placed his eiruv «outside» the city’s «outskirts,» i.e., beyond the area of slightly more than seventy cubits surrounding the city, the eiruv is effective in establishing his Shabbat residence at that location."
  }
 ],
